tasks.official_scoring_standard:
Execution-based scoring: run the submitted solution and verify it meets the success criteria below. The single defining gradable scalar is the stealth invariant delta_J = |J(x_a) - J(x)| ~= 0 (a correct a=H*c attack leaves the weighted residual unchanged to machine precision; a naive/wrong tamper produces a large delta_J and J(x_a) >> chi2_threshold, i.e. it is detected). Award the four DERBench L3 capability dimensions (Information Extraction, Domain Reasoning, Multi-Objective Decision Making, Uncertainty & Adaptation), 0-25 each (max 100), based on correctness, method validity, and completeness.

Success criteria: {"attack_must_bypass_chi2_test": true, "corrupted_state_must_differ_from_true": true, "must_report": ["H_matrix_shape_and_rank", "attack_vector_a", "state_perturbation_c", "true_state_vs_corrupted_state", "J_x_before_attack", "J_x_after_attack", "chi2_threshold", "residual_analysis"], "must_demonstrate": "The corrupted measurements pass the Chi-squared test (J(x_a) < threshold) while the estimated state is meaningfully different from the true state"}

Reference solution: The implementation should demonstrate: (1) A valid pandapower network with state estimation converging on clean measurements with J(x) well below the Chi-squared threshold (typically J(x) ~ 3-8 for the expected degrees of freedom vs threshold of ~15-20). (2) The H matrix should be extracted as an m x n matrix where m = number of measurements (typically 16-20) and n = number of state variables (12-13 for a 13-bus system). The matrix should have full column rank for observability. (3) The attack vector a = Hc should be computed for a chosen c that perturbs 1-2 bus voltage angles/magnitudes by 0.01-0.03 pu. Because a lies in the column space of H, the state estimator will find a new state x_a = x_true + c that perfectly explains the corrupted measurements, producing residuals identical to the pre-attack case. (4) The post-attack J(x_a) should be nearly identical to J(x) (within numerical precision), confirming the Chi-squared test is bypassed. (5) The voltage at targeted buses should show the intended perturbation (e.g., Bus 671 voltage estimated as 1.005 pu instead of true 0.990 pu). This demonstrates the fundamental vulnerability identified by Liu, Ning, and Reiter (2011): with knowledge of H, an attacker can construct undetectable measurement corruptions.
